    "result_text": "The full test suite passes \u2014 **52 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**, including the new `Cp38Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist in the owner-creation endpoint (`POST /api/owners`), handled by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\nChanges in `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`:\n\n1. **Blocklist constant** \u2014 a `Set<String> DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` containing `mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`.\n2. **Rejection check** \u2014 in `addOwner`, alongside the other 400-level validations, the request is rejected with `400 BAD_REQUEST` when the owner's email domain is on the blocklist.\n3. **Helper `isDisposableEmailDomain`** \u2014 extracts the domain (part after the last `@`), normalizes it (trim + lowercase, matching the app's existing email-normalization idiom), and checks membership. Null/malformed emails pass through (no domain to block), so owners without an email are unaffected.\n\nThe check sits before persistence and before the duplicate/quota logic, so disposable-domain owners are rejected cleanly without side effects.",
